WEBVTT

00:05.980 --> 00:10.860
23:28            In Front of Shibuya Stream

00:31.870 --> 00:33.880
Kusakabe?

00:35.600 --> 00:39.630
Hey! Kusakabe!

00:47.300 --> 00:49.250
Found you!

00:51.940 --> 00:53.720
Panda.

00:53.720 --> 00:56.740
This is awfully different from what I heard.

00:56.740 --> 00:57.730
Huh?

00:58.110 --> 00:59.960
About Itadori.

01:00.320 --> 01:02.250
Nah, that was Sukuna.

01:02.250 --> 01:04.960
Itadori holds control over that body.

01:06.080 --> 01:08.050
That's the current story, right?

01:08.050 --> 01:09.320
Urk.

01:12.360 --> 01:14.180
I'll tell you this now.

01:15.200 --> 01:20.470
No matter what judgment gets doled out 
to Itadori later now that Gojo is gone,

01:20.810 --> 01:23.200
I won't be taking your side.

01:28.400 --> 01:31.740
I'm in favor of Yuji Itadori's execution.

01:33.110 --> 01:37.110
22:36       (Local Time)
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hMalaysia, Kuala Lumpur

01:41.480 --> 01:43.310
Sorry about that.

01:43.970 --> 01:46.370
You must be worn out, Ui Ui.

01:46.900 --> 01:50.760
Shall we sleep in the same bed tonight?

01:50.760 --> 01:53.880
What?! That's so improper!

01:55.470 --> 01:57.870
Do you hate me when I'm improper?

01:57.870 --> 01:58.880
No way!

01:59.440 --> 02:02.280
Sorry, I got a call back.

02:02.280 --> 02:04.640
Oh, Nee-sama...

02:06.040 --> 02:08.110
Sorry for calling so late.

02:09.160 --> 02:11.580
Oh, right, it's morning where you are.

02:12.480 --> 02:13.660
Me?

02:14.050 --> 02:15.360
In KL.

02:17.180 --> 02:19.900
Yes, with Ui Ui's Technique.

02:20.410 --> 02:22.880
We nearly got ourselves killed, after all.

02:23.860 --> 02:28.850
You should sell off any stocks in Japan 
and all your real estate in Tokyo.

02:29.370 --> 02:31.710
I've already exchanged all of my yen.

02:32.620 --> 02:35.490
Yes, do it right away.

02:36.660 --> 02:41.120
I doubt any of the major developed nations 
will be spared from these negative events.

02:41.120 --> 02:46.260
Japan is still the world's 
#3 economy, despite all else.

02:47.380 --> 02:49.920
Well, I'll leave the arrangements up to you.

02:50.900 --> 02:53.560
It's fine. You don't need to thank me.

02:53.560 --> 02:56.400
Just keep me on the inside, like usual.

03:00.410 --> 03:02.880
I look forward to working with you again.

03:04.530 --> 03:07.350
Bread, bread, bread!

03:07.350 --> 03:08.910
What's wrong, Nii-chan?

03:09.310 --> 03:10.790
Not feeling well?

03:21.680 --> 03:24.700
23:28           Shibuya Station
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hB3F, Denentoshin Line Platform

03:24.100 --> 03:25.700
I have to go.

03:28.090 --> 03:30.330
Yuji Itadori...

03:30.330 --> 03:32.710
What are you?

03:35.690 --> 03:37.600
I have to know.

03:39.360 --> 03:44.010
What am I?

03:46.360 --> 03:48.370
Shall I save you,

03:48.370 --> 03:51.370
23:36            Shibuya Police Station, Udagawa Police Box Ruins

03:48.630 --> 03:49.720
Mahito?

03:59.570 --> 04:01.810
Did he just say Geto?!

04:02.470 --> 04:03.700
Give him back!

04:04.320 --> 04:07.680
Give us back Gojo-sensei!

04:08.270 --> 04:10.950
People believed catfish were 
connected to earthquakes

04:10.950 --> 04:13.910
and told stories of such a monster 
up until the mid-Edo era.

04:14.470 --> 04:17.210
They believed that when this 
"Onamazu" moved underground,

04:17.210 --> 04:20.040
it caused earthquakes to occur.

04:31.020 --> 04:32.870
What just happened?!

04:34.160 --> 04:36.200
You thought you fell in, didn't you?

04:36.720 --> 04:41.640
Though, from the outside, it looked 
like you fell back all on your own.

04:43.560 --> 04:46.960
The greatest strength of Cursed Spirit 
Manipulation is its quantity of options.

04:47.470 --> 04:50.800
I can utilize multiple cursed 
spirits semi-first-grade or higher,

04:51.030 --> 04:54.770
and even if you analyze and 
overcome their techniques,

04:54.770 --> 04:57.280
I can just send out new 
cursed spirits again.

04:58.890 --> 05:03.150
Of course, I can also simply pile on 
attacks without giving you time for that.

05:11.950 --> 05:13.560
This won't...

05:21.230 --> 05:23.120
If his forces hadn't been divided

05:23.120 --> 05:27.770
across Kyoto and Shinjuku during last 
year's Night Parade of a Hundred Demons,

05:27.770 --> 05:30.710
he would have won instead of Okkotsu.

05:31.690 --> 05:35.010
Though, I suppose that had nothing 
to do with you, did it?

05:37.280 --> 05:38.730
Give him back!

05:39.140 --> 05:42.060
I suppose I should say that 
even I am impressed.

05:42.060 --> 05:45.570
Sukuna's vessel... is tough.

05:49.440 --> 05:51.040
I knew that.

05:51.560 --> 05:56.880
After all, I was born from you humans.

06:35.340 --> 06:36.950
Shall we continue...

06:39.390 --> 06:41.880
our discussion of the world to come?

06:42.960 --> 06:45.960
Episode 46
Metamorphosis, Part 2

06:56.520 --> 07:01.040
JUJUTSU KAISEN
Shibuya Incident

08:18.010 --> 08:21.050
Do you know about what 
they call a "Supreme Art"?

08:24.780 --> 08:27.120
It's very much akin to 
the ultimate expression

08:27.120 --> 08:29.320
of a cursed technique, 
aside from one's domain.

08:32.840 --> 08:36.280
The Supreme Art of Cursed 
Spirit Manipulation is Uzumaki.

08:36.750 --> 08:39.190
This combines the absorbed 
cursed spirits into one,

08:39.190 --> 08:42.530
creating super-high-density cursed energy 
to attack your opponent with.

08:51.320 --> 08:53.930
What are you laughing about?

08:54.840 --> 08:56.880
Oh, sorry.

08:56.880 --> 09:00.620
I just realized I had started acting like him.

09:01.310 --> 09:03.310
We were talking about Uzumaki, yes?

09:04.420 --> 09:06.460
Uzumaki is powerful,

09:06.460 --> 09:08.440
but it also means throwing 
away the quantity

09:08.440 --> 09:11.440
of options that serves as Cursed Spirit 
Manipulation's main strength.

09:11.440 --> 09:14.640
So it wasn't very tempting to me at first.

09:15.240 --> 09:19.230
After all, I thought it was just a way 
to recycle low-level cursed spirits.

09:24.660 --> 09:26.350
But I was wrong.

09:26.600 --> 09:28.040
It displays its true value

09:28.040 --> 09:32.510
when a cursed spirit above 
semi-first-grade is used in Uzumaki—

09:32.960 --> 09:36.570
and their technique is extracted.

09:47.960 --> 09:49.640
How foolish.

09:50.440 --> 09:55.420
Did you think I wouldn't notice 
the presence you felt?

10:00.280 --> 10:01.360
Our signal!

10:01.360 --> 10:02.490
The target is...

10:02.840 --> 10:04.600
right below Nishimiya!

10:23.990 --> 10:24.870
Tsk.

10:26.180 --> 10:28.220
A sniper rifle, huh?

10:28.220 --> 10:29.450
Nice.

10:30.000 --> 10:32.610
I also agree that conventional weapons

10:32.610 --> 10:36.540
should be proactively used 
when fighting a jujutsu sorcerer.

10:37.230 --> 10:40.410
Back when I was captain 
of the youth basketball team,

10:40.410 --> 10:44.160
I remember my mother would 
often dye my hair black.

10:44.920 --> 10:47.270
In middle school, I met my mentor,

10:47.270 --> 10:48.890
and I chose to become a jujutsu sorcerer

10:48.890 --> 10:51.670
before ever holding a wooden 
or a bamboo sword in my hands,

10:51.670 --> 10:53.920
let alone a real sword.

10:55.040 --> 10:57.410
I swung my sword relentlessly.

10:57.680 --> 11:00.600
Because I didn't want to be 
a burden on my mother.

11:02.320 --> 11:04.640
I swung my sword relentlessly.

11:08.140 --> 11:10.360
Because I didn't want to die.

11:11.070 --> 11:12.940
New Shadow Style...

11:13.160 --> 11:14.490
Put it all in!

11:15.310 --> 11:17.320
Everything I've experienced,

11:17.320 --> 11:19.360
as well as my future to come!

11:19.720 --> 11:23.750
Even if it means I'll never 
swing a sword again!

11:24.080 --> 11:25.440
Quick Draw!

11:38.360 --> 11:39.860
Supreme Art:

11:42.880 --> 11:44.740
Uzumaki.

11:46.680 --> 11:47.860
Wait!

12:09.440 --> 12:11.440
New Shadow Style, huh?

12:11.440 --> 12:13.080
I'm glad.

12:13.690 --> 12:16.760
It's nice facing someone 
with a bit of knowledge.

12:22.860 --> 12:24.570
Kusakabe-san!

12:24.790 --> 12:27.630
There's no point if you're 
out in front, Sensei!

12:27.630 --> 12:29.290
I couldn't help it!

12:33.470 --> 12:35.730
Itadori...

12:35.730 --> 12:37.680
It's you, right?

12:38.280 --> 12:39.760
Panda-senpai!

12:38.980 --> 12:40.190
And the Kyoto students!!

12:40.190 --> 12:43.570
Good, you're back to normal.

12:41.360 --> 12:43.570
I'm in Gorilla mode.

12:43.850 --> 12:46.110
That man has Satoru Gojo...

12:46.470 --> 12:48.770
and the Prison Realm, huh?

12:48.770 --> 12:50.240
Apparently.

12:50.240 --> 12:53.920
I don't know what he finds so fun about 
walking around with that public nuisance.

12:54.340 --> 12:55.460
Who is he?

12:55.730 --> 12:57.870
The shell is Suguru Geto.

12:57.870 --> 13:00.190
I don't know what's inside.

13:15.580 --> 13:17.610
Hey, Choso.

13:19.480 --> 13:21.090
He's...

13:27.620 --> 13:30.610
I have three parents.

13:30.610 --> 13:31.900
My mother,

13:31.900 --> 13:34.100
the cursed spirit that 
impregnated my mother,

13:34.100 --> 13:37.090
and the man who mixed his 
blood into the affair...

13:37.840 --> 13:40.440
The one who toyed with my mother...

13:40.440 --> 13:42.160
The loathsome—

13:42.620 --> 13:44.420
Looks like you've realized it.

13:44.810 --> 13:46.930
So that's how it is!

13:47.850 --> 13:50.440
Kamo Noritoshi!

13:50.690 --> 13:51.810
Kamo?!

13:51.810 --> 13:53.140
Noritoshi?!

13:52.830 --> 13:54.560
Kamo Noritoshi

13:53.140 --> 13:54.560
Me?!

13:54.830 --> 13:55.960
What?!

13:55.960 --> 13:57.320
What's going on?!

13:57.320 --> 13:58.940
The stain on the Kamo clan!

13:58.940 --> 14:00.960
The worst sorcerer in all history!

14:01.800 --> 14:06.320
If he's right, then whatever's inside 
Geto would be over 150 years old.

14:07.610 --> 14:09.870
Outlandish barriers,

14:09.870 --> 14:12.710
and possession of outlandish cursed tools...

14:12.710 --> 14:17.200
As far as masterminds with a cursed 
technique to take over other bodies goes...

14:17.490 --> 14:19.450
That seems appropriate, yeah.

14:20.520 --> 14:24.240
Kamo Noritoshi is merely one 
of the many names I've had.

14:24.240 --> 14:25.830
Call me whatever you like.

14:27.040 --> 14:28.560
How dare you...

14:29.510 --> 14:31.220
How dare you make me

14:31.220 --> 14:33.230
try to kill Itadori?!

14:33.230 --> 14:37.140
My little brother!

14:41.450 --> 14:43.590
Stand down, third-rate.

14:43.590 --> 14:45.930
Don't keep me waiting any longer.

14:45.930 --> 14:47.190
Move it!

14:47.190 --> 14:49.600
I'm his older brother!

14:52.410 --> 14:54.990
JUJUTSU KAISEN

14:52.410 --> 14:54.990
JUJUTSU KAISEN

14:58.200 --> 15:00.000
JUJUTSU KAISEN

14:58.200 --> 15:00.000
JUJUTSU KAISEN

15:07.540 --> 15:10.160
It's a side effect of my technique.

15:10.910 --> 15:13.820
I can feel any changes to 
my blood-related siblings,

15:13.820 --> 15:16.720
no matter how far away they are.

15:26.540 --> 15:28.440
My younger brothers died.

15:29.190 --> 15:30.360
Death.

15:30.360 --> 15:32.200
For every living being,

15:32.200 --> 15:35.200
that is their last and greatest change.

15:35.760 --> 15:37.950
In that moment,

15:38.270 --> 15:42.650
I strongly sensed the death of 
Yuji Itadori, right before my eyes.

15:44.360 --> 15:46.040
Which means that Yuji

15:46.040 --> 15:48.940
must also be my 
blood-related younger brother!

15:51.350 --> 15:54.200
If Kamo Noritoshi has 
been extending his life

15:54.200 --> 15:56.430
by transferring bodies,

15:56.430 --> 15:58.920
then it's not an impossible idea.

16:00.030 --> 16:01.840
Which means I...

16:03.400 --> 16:04.800
must use my full strength

16:04.800 --> 16:07.070
to perform my duty as the older brother!

16:07.520 --> 16:09.680
Blood Manipulation?!

16:13.120 --> 16:14.910
So much pressure!

16:19.960 --> 16:21.480
It's fast!

16:21.480 --> 16:23.590
So this is Piercing Blood?!

16:59.050 --> 17:00.120
Tsk!

18:27.030 --> 18:28.850
Don't push yourself too hard.

18:28.850 --> 18:30.580
You're exhausted, aren't you?

18:32.480 --> 18:34.010
So what?

18:35.360 --> 18:37.760
Is that any reason not to risk my life

18:37.760 --> 18:40.840
for the younger brother 
right in front of me?

18:44.400 --> 18:47.680
Just asking, but you two 
are strangers, right?

18:48.100 --> 18:51.130
Worse than strangers.
He nearly killed me once already.

18:51.600 --> 18:53.350
First it was Todo.

18:53.350 --> 18:56.200
Are you sure you aren't emitting 
dangerous pheromones or something?

18:57.640 --> 18:59.860
Still, thanks to him, 
the fight has grown chaotic.

19:00.250 --> 19:02.050
We're taking advantage of this.

19:02.050 --> 19:03.250
Right.

19:03.250 --> 19:06.420
I still have two cores, 
so I'll lead in the front.

19:06.420 --> 19:09.630
If we all attack him together, 
it should at least create an opening.

19:10.450 --> 19:13.710
We must do everything we can 
to steal back the Prison Realm.

19:21.650 --> 19:24.020
Drumming—

19:24.400 --> 19:26.140
Ice Formation:

19:26.760 --> 19:28.400
Frost Calm!

19:34.900 --> 19:36.750
An ice cursed technique?!

19:36.750 --> 19:38.900
And one this high-level?!

19:38.900 --> 19:42.030
If I move, I'll shatter my body!

19:45.030 --> 19:46.070
Tsk!

19:47.080 --> 19:48.520
Don't kill them.

19:48.520 --> 19:50.650
I need messengers.

19:50.650 --> 19:53.040
Is that any reason to leave them all alive?

19:56.670 --> 19:58.780
A reverse cursed technique!

19:58.780 --> 20:01.780
Their sorcery is on a different scale.

20:01.780 --> 20:03.690
I want to go home!

20:04.330 --> 20:06.680
This ice isn't enough!

20:06.680 --> 20:09.000
Flowing Red Scale!

20:12.600 --> 20:14.750
Then how much is?

20:22.610 --> 20:24.580
Whose body do you think that is?!

20:24.580 --> 20:26.810
I was the only one not frozen as solid!

20:26.810 --> 20:28.470
Must have to do with Sukuna!

20:29.460 --> 20:31.000
You're our ally, right?

20:31.000 --> 20:31.960
No!

20:31.960 --> 20:32.960
Huh?!

20:33.360 --> 20:35.590
I'm your older brother.

20:35.970 --> 20:38.100
Could you please take this seriously?!

20:38.100 --> 20:40.830
Why don't you try saying 
it once, for starters?

20:40.830 --> 20:42.480
Call me "Onii-chan."

20:43.940 --> 20:45.760
Tool Manipulation:

20:46.630 --> 20:48.430
Wind Scythe!

20:50.990 --> 20:52.030
Shit!

20:52.030 --> 20:54.770
It's depressing that they parried 
it with their bare hands!

20:55.180 --> 20:56.600
Itadori-kun!

20:56.600 --> 20:58.910
We're the only ones who can move right now!

20:58.910 --> 21:02.530
We need to buy time for Utahime-sensei 
to finish her preparations!

21:03.000 --> 21:05.120
Yuji Itadori

21:06.540 --> 21:10.110
is the only messenger you need, right?!

21:11.120 --> 21:14.160
Ice Formation: Icefall!

21:26.180 --> 21:26.930
We're gonna die!

21:34.120 --> 21:36.210
Long time no see,

21:36.210 --> 21:37.670
Geto-kun.

21:40.410 --> 21:43.920
Could I get your answer to 
my question from back then?

21:45.910 --> 21:48.640
What kind of woman is your type?

21:51.640 --> 21:53.720
Yuki Tsukumo!

23:25.550 --> 23:28.480
When one person's happiness conflicts 
with another person's happiness,

23:28.480 --> 23:30.470
that's when unhappiness is born,

23:30.470 --> 23:32.220
but when two people's unhappiness conflicts,

23:32.220 --> 23:35.160
it usually only creates 
more unhappiness, you know?

23:35.160 --> 23:37.290
Next time, "Shibuya Incident: Gate Closed."

23:35.160 --> 23:41.930
Next Episode
Shibuya Incident: Gate Closed

23:37.290 --> 23:39.600
I just want to crawl into a warm bed and sleep.
